.TH HELIOGRAPH 1 "" "Heliograph" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
heliograph \- a fast, private media library and player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B heliograph
[\fB\-\-add\fR] [\fB\-\-tab\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-window\fR] [\fIPATH\fR ...]
.br
.B heliograph
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Heliograph
browses and plays large collections of pictures, videos and music. It loads only what is on the screen,
keeps its index in a local SQLite database, plays formats that browsers cannot (MOV, MKV, HEVC and more)
by repackaging or converting them with FFmpeg, and converts pictures, video and audio.
Everything stays on this computer: it listens on 127.0.0.1 only and has no telemetry.
.PP
The window is a Chromium\-based browser in app mode. A small background service is started when needed
and stops by itself after a while without use.
.PP
Without a command,
.B heliograph
opens the window. Give it a folder to browse everything inside it, or a picture, video or audio file to
view it (the files next to it are one arrow key away). A folder is only browsed for now, unless
.B \-\-add
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
These apply when opening folders and files.
.TP
.B \-\-add
Add the folders to the library instead of only opening them.
.TP
.B \-\-tab
Open in the default browser instead of an app window.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-window
Only start the service and index the folders.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help. Every command also has its own \fB\-\-help\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B cache
[\fBsize\fR|\fBprune\fR|\fBclear\fR]: thumbnail cache usage, pruning and clearing.
.TP
.B config
[\fIkey\fR [\fIvalue\fR]] [\fB\-\-json\fR]: show or change settings. Changes apply at once.
.TP
.B convert
[\fB\-\-to\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-\-quality\fR \fIhigh|balanced|small\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-height\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR] \fIFILE\fR ...: convert
pictures, videos and audio with FFmpeg. Originals are never changed or overwritten. \fB\-\-list\fR shows every preset.
.TP
.B default
[\fB\-\-images\fR] [\fB\-\-videos\fR] [\fB\-\-audio\fR] [\fB\-\-folders\fR]: make Heliograph the default application for those
types. The previous defaults are remembered; \fB\-\-restore\fR undoes the change and \fB\-\-status\fR shows the current state.
.TP
.B doctor
Check that everything Heliograph needs works (Python, FFmpeg, a browser, optional tools).
.TP
.B formats
What Heliograph indexes and what this machine can decode.
.TP
.B info
\fIFILE\fR: show what is inside a media file and how it plays.
.TP
.B install
Add Heliograph to the app menu and to "Open with" for this user. It does not change any default.
\fB\-\-uninstall\fR removes it again. Packages already install a menu entry; run this once on Wayland to make the
launcher match the window's class.
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP server on standard input and output so AI assistants can search and inspect the library
(read\-only unless \fB\-\-allow\-convert\fR is given).
.TP
.B monitor
Live terminal status of the service. \fB\-\-once\fR prints one frame and exits.
.TP
.B rescan
Rescan the library folders (needs the service to be running).
.TP
.B search
[\fB\-\-kind\fR \fIimage|video|audio\fR] [\fB\-\-in\fR \fIFOLDER\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIWORDS\fR ...: search the
library from the terminal. Read\-only; no service needed.
.TP
.B serve
Run the service in the foreground.
.TP
.B status
Service status; \fB\-\-json\fR for scripts.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the background service.
.TP
.B version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/heliograph/
The library database (folders, file details, favourites, settings) and a small recovery snapshot.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/heliograph/
Thumbnails and previews. A cache: safe to delete.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/heliograph/
The running service's details and its log.
.PP
The locations follow XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME and XDG_STATE_HOME. To remove everything Heliograph stored,
run \fBheliograph stop\fR and delete those three folders.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HELIOGRAPH_BROWSER
Command (with arguments) of the browser to use for the window instead of the first Chromium\-based browser found.
.TP
.B HELIOGRAPH_HOME
Keep all data, cache and state under this folder instead of the XDG locations. Useful for trying things out.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the command failed (the reason is printed on standard error).
.SH BUGS
Report problems at https://github.com/md8-habibullah/heliograph/issues
